          "filename": "Boat to Kisimul Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1365709.jpg",
          "caption": "Boat to Kisimul Castle Historic Scotland leases Kisimul Castle from the Macneils; it is open to visitors, and access is by boat leaving every 30 minutes from this slipway (the crossing is included in the admission price).  The outward journey is quick and very direct; the more scenic route back to the jetty goes around the south and west faces of the Castle. I was the only passenger on this particular sailing and managed to practice a bit of Gaelic with the crew!",
          "alt": "Boat to Kisimul Castle Historic Scotland leases Kisimul Castle from the Macneils; it is open to visitors, and access is by boat leaving every 30 minutes from this slipway (the crossing is included in the admission price).  The outward journey is quick and very direct; the more scenic route back to the jetty goes around the south and west faces of the Castle. I was the only passenger on this particular sailing and managed to practice a bit of Gaelic with the crew!",
